After the first version of this went a bit sideways (thanks Fuji), I went about making this again. 
A fan favourite named after a guitarist, it's no longer available in the UK but is in the US (sorry, I don't know about other locations). 

It's a Cherry Ice Cream with Cherry pieces and either chocolate chunks (uk) or fudge flecks (US) depending on where you are. 

What you'll need:

240ml cream (50% fat)
300ml milk (1.8% fat)
80g sugar
60g Cherry concentrate 
2tsp Cherry liqueur if wanted
2tbsp Skimmed Milk Powder
50g chopped (70% chocolate) 
50g maraschino cherries chopped (use Luxardo but Ben & Jerry's use Bing Cherries)

The type of cherries have a big impact on the flavour so you can change the base just by changing the cherry. 

